docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-556-
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md:557:- `ProceduralGround` is shared by Jungle, Showroom, Plaza, and Terrain/clearing. Indexed smooth normals fix SwiftShader faceting but can alter all lighting. Keep option boundaries, update all ground/terrain specs, and run full suite.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-558-- `ProjectScene` mounts shared Terminal, SeedLever, CommitRidge, LanguagePillars, ReleaseMarkers, and StarLanterns. Skin through options/data, never Deslopify-only branches in generic constructors. Run project placement tests for every project.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-559-- `Sun`, `Mood`, `PostStack`, camera rig, capability tiers, and scene director are global. Scope Jungle-specific values and prove current defaults for other worlds.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-560-- Existing scene-director demo capture can suppress movement/E. World-mode input must be explicit and regression-tested.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md:561:- Dynamic prompts update on engine tick. Stable interactable objects with mutable prompt/callback are safer than replacing objects each frame.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-562-
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md:563:### SwiftShader and headless tests
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-564-
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md:565:- SwiftShader/llvmpipe may lack WebGL2, derivatives, half-float targets, or reliable font metrics. Use capability guards, current shader fallback patterns, and canvas text fallbacks.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-566-- Current ground was faceted because nonindexed geometry/per-face colours masked normal issues. Inspect indexed buffers and shader strings rather than require GPU screenshots.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-567-- Avoid exact screenshot assertions for antialiasing, font rasterization, fog, and bloom. Assert dimensions, uniforms, state, and stable text.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-568-- Run focused Angular specs with `--watch=false`; run browser gate separately.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-569-
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-570-### Performance and budget
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-571-
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-572-- Initial gzip script budget is `350 kB` in `scripts/check-budget.mjs`. No dependencies. Keep flow/data dynamically imported with project route where current architecture allows.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md:573:- Use instancing for plants/canopy/fireflies, shared geometry/materials, capped counts, and exact tiers. Dispose card/tag textures and flow objects.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-574-- High post-processing is opt-in. Preserve composer cap `1.5`, AO/bloom limits, and low/medium post off.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-575-- Avoid animation-loop allocations: cache vectors, uniforms, progress state, and event throttles.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md:576:- Four cards at 640×600 plus four tags at 512×240 consume texture memory. Reuse contexts where possible, dispose on exit, and retain only needed transition textures.
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-577-
docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-deslopify-jungle-design.md-578-### Reduced motion and mobile
