     5	/**
     6	 * The Deslopify jungle laid out in world metres: two banks either side of a stream, one bridge
     7	 * across it under the arch, and every spot the flow furnishes. The source is the top-down flow
     8	 * prototype (#2a of the design handoff), a 960 × 680 pixel map; `mapToWorld` is the one
     9	 * conversion from its pixels to this world, so every anchor below is written in map pixels and
    10	 * read in metres. Only positions convert. Sizes are physical (a card is 2.1 m wide, not the map's
    11	 * 34 px icon), and rates and radii stay the flow's business.
    12	 *
    13	 * Nothing here knows about three.js scenes: the environment builds from it, and the flow places
    14	 * its lantern, cards, vines and tags on it. Every exported point is frozen; clone before changing.
    15	 */
    16	
